('Queen Elizabeth Islands','Queen Elizabeth Islands',NULL,NULL,'unattested',NULL,'multiword,capitalized','["proper noun"]','An archipelago that is a component of the Canadian Arctic Archipelago, the northern islands north of the Parry Channel (the Straight East-West Northwest Passage), west of the Nares Strait, and bounded on the north and west by the Arctic Ocean.','proper noun','From Queen Elizabeth + islands.
Named after Elizabeth II, Queen of Canada; renamed in honour of her coronation as Queen (Empress) of the British Empire. The island cluster was formerly the Parry Islands / Parry Archipelago, which subsequently were restricted to referring to the southernmost islands of the island cluster, running along the Parry Channel.',355,'200plus',0,0.64,50),
('thromboendoarterioectomy','thromboendoarterioectomy',NULL,'/ˌθɹɒmbəʊˌɛndəʊɑːˌtɪəɹɪəʊˈɛktəmɪ/','marginal',NULL,'pointer_only','["noun"]','Rare spelling of thrombendarteriectomy.','noun','Formed as thrombo- + endo- + arteri- + -o- + -ectomy; compare the better-formed thrombendarteriectomy and see thrombendarteriectomy.',132,'120_200',0,0.55,51),
