('culinarily challenged','culinarily challenged',NULL,NULL,'rare',NULL,'multiword','["adjective"]','Unable to cook.','adjective','An ironic imitation of the perceived oversensitivity of language like mentally challenged.',90,'80_120',0,0.5,55),
('withdrive','withdrive',NULL,NULL,'marginal',-1.24,'plain','["verb"]','To drive away, repel.','verb','From Middle English *withdriven, from Old English wiþdrīfan (“to repel”), from Proto-West Germanic *wiþidrīban (“to drive back”), equivalent to with- + drive. Cognate with Old Frisian withdrīva (“to restore”). Compare also Old High German widartrīban (“to drive back, refute”), whence archaic German widertreiben (“to drive back, prevent, thwart”).',348,'200plus',1,0.8,56),
