('Pontic','Pontic',NULL,'/ˈpɒntɪk/','scarce',1.86,'capitalized','["adjective", "proper noun"]','Of or relating to Pontic Greek, the dialect of Greek that developed in Pontus and is now spoken chiefly in rural northern Greece.','adjective','From Latin ponticus, from Ancient Greek Ποντῐκός (Pontĭkós), from Πόντος (Póntos, “Black Sea, Pontus”) + -ικός (-ikós, “-ic: forming adjectives”). Equivalent to Pontus + -ic. Doublet of bonduc and bundook.',205,'200plus',1,0.74,66),
