('e:3d092fe567af256b4f36f6042df17452db6d0fafc10fd72ccb3e9bc492675af6','tack',5,'/tæk/','common',3.56,'plain','["noun"]','A contract by which the use of a thing is set, or let, for hire; a lease.','noun','From Middle English tak, take (“fee, tax (on livestock)”), from Old Norse tak, taka (“a taking, seizure; revenue”), from Old Norse taka (“to take”). Cognate with Scots tack.',173,'120_200',1,0.8,72),
