('since','since',NULL,'/sɪn(t)s/','common',5.75,'plain','["adverb", "preposition", "conjunction"]','From a specified time in the past.','adverb','From Middle English syns, synnes, contraction of earlier sithens, sithence, from sithen (“after, since”) ( + -s, adverbial genitive suffix), from Old English sīþþan, from the phrase sīþ þǣm (“after/since that (time)”), from sīþ (“since, after”) + þǣm dative singular of þæt. Cognate with Dutch sinds (“since”), German seit (“since”), Danish siden (“since”), Icelandic síðan (“since”) Scots syne (“since”).',405,'200plus',1,0.8,197),
