('copula','copula',NULL,'/ˈkɑpjələ/','uncommon',2.91,'plain','["noun"]','A word, usually a verb, used to link the subject of a sentence with a predicate (usually a subject complement or an adverbial), that unites or associates the subject with the predicate.','noun','Borrowed from Latin cōpula (“connection, linking of words”), from co- (“together”) + apere (“fasten”). Doublet of couple.',121,'120_200',1,0.78,321),
('e:dcb712aec35c0154169f7934d4d28dc2779d43700d1b81fafede4b59e0010677','Sabir',3,'/sɑˈbiɹ/','scarce',1.9,'capitalized','["proper noun"]','A male given name from Arabic.','proper noun','Ultimately from Arabic صَابِر (ṣābir).',38,'lt40',1,0.35,322),
('Margherita','Margherita',NULL,NULL,'uncommon',2.56,'capitalized,pointer_only','["noun"]','Synonym of margherita pizza (“A pizza made with tomato, mozzarella cheese, and basil.”).','noun','From Italian Margherita, supposedly named after Margherita of Savoy (1851–1926); see margherita pizza. Doublet of Margaret (and various forms, q.v.), margarita, margarite, and marguerite.',187,'120_200',1,0.78,323),
('Potato Germans','Potato Germans',NULL,NULL,'rare',NULL,'multiword,capitalized','["noun"]','A group of German families who settled in the heathlands of central Jutland in Denmark during the mid-1700s.','noun','Calque of Danish Kartoffeltyskere, in reference to the cultivation of potatoes in the areas they settled.',105,'80_120',1,0.55,324),
('laughter','laughter',NULL,'/ˈlæftɚ/','common',4.2,'plain','["noun"]','The sound of laughing, produced by air so expelled; any similar sound.','noun','From Middle English laughter, laghter, laȝter, from Old English hleahtor (“laughter, jubilation, derision”), from Proto-Germanic *hlahtraz (“laughter”), from Proto-Indo-European *klek-, *kleg- (“to shout”). Cognate with German Gelächter (“laughter, hilarity, merriment”), Danish and Norwegian latter (“laughter”), Icelandic hlátur (“laughter”). More at laugh.',359,'200plus',1,0.8,325),
('Hentland','Hentland',NULL,NULL,'unattested',NULL,'capitalized','["proper noun"]','A hamlet and civil parish (served by Ballingham, Bolstone and Hentland Group Parish Council) in south Herefordshire, England (OS grid ref SO5426).','proper noun','From Old Welsh.',15,'lt40',1,0.3,326),
('e:a1baa4a6f3253b8a829155e9e8574063ab3cca29a25cfce0b4082096edc6693a','push',2,'/pʊʃ/','common',4.86,'plain','["noun"]','A pustule; a pimple.','noun','Probably French poche. See pouch.',33,'lt40',1,0.4,327),
('Conflent','Conflent',NULL,NULL,'unattested',NULL,'capitalized','["proper noun"]','A comarca in Northern Catalonia.','proper noun','From Catalan Conflent.',22,'lt40',1,0.3,328),
('fabricate','fabricate',NULL,'/ˈfæb.ɹɪ.keɪt/','common',3.88,'plain','["verb"]','To form into a whole by uniting its parts; to construct; to build.','verb','From Middle English fabricaten (“to fashion, make”), from Latin fabricātus, perfect active participle of fabricor (see -ate (verb-forming suffix)), from fabrica (“a fabric, building”) + -or (verb-forming suffix); see fabric and forge. Cognate with French fabriquer.',265,'200plus',1,0.8,329),
('anorectin','anorectin',NULL,NULL,'marginal',-1.23,'plain','["noun"]','A peptide that reduces eating in mammals. The sequence of amino acids is Pyr-Val-Asp-Ser-Met-Trp-Ala-Glu-Gln-Lys-Gln-Met-Glu-Leu-Glu-Ser-Ile-Leu-Val-Ala-Leu-Leu-Gln-Lys-His-Ser-Arg-Asn-Ser-Gln-NH2','noun','* Appears in "Effects on Feeding Behavior of Rats of a Cryptic Peptide from the C-Terminal End of Prepro-Growth Hormone-Releasing Factor" K. ARASE, T. SAKAGUCHI, M. TAKAHASHI, G. A. BRAY, N. LING
Endocrinology, Volume 121, Issue 6, 1 December 1987, Pages 1960–1965, https://doi.org/10.1210/endo-121-6-1960',305,'200plus',1,0.6,330),
('attentisme','attentisme',NULL,NULL,'rare',0.39,'plain','["noun"]','A policy of waiting; a waiting game.','noun','Borrowed from French attentisme.',32,'lt40',1,0.39,331),
('ipamorelin','ipamorelin',NULL,NULL,'obscure',-0.54,'plain','["noun"]','A growth hormone–releasing hormone analogue.','noun','Random prefix suffixed with -morelin (“growth hormone release–stimulating peptide”).',84,'80_120',1,0.5,332),
