('kaffir corn','kaffir corn',NULL,NULL,'unattested',NULL,'multiword','["noun"]','Sorghum cultivars (Sorghum bicolor vars.), used as a food for people and animals and in ethanol production.','noun','This name for sorghum is probably connected with both the distinction of Muslim versus non-Muslim and the distinction of sub-Saharan Black race versus other race; the history of usage of the word kaffir includes derogation, depending on time and place. For more information, see kaffir cabbage and see the Wikipedia article on kaffir as a racial term.',351,'200plus',0,0.6,409),
