('demolish','demolish',NULL,'/dɪˈmɒl.ɪʃ/','common',3.52,'plain','["verb"]','To destroy (buildings, etc.), especially in a planned or intentional fashion.','verb','Attested since the 16th century; from Middle French demoliss-, the stem of some conjugated forms of the verb demolir (“to destroy”, “to tear down”), from Latin dēmōlior (“to tear down”). Displaced native Old English tōweorpan (literally “to throw apart”).',255,'200plus',1,0.8,412),
