('e:07d582085d7b20aaa0d2d74f4995c643ce5f181e220a7917638edc7e61753a8f','tent',3,'/tɛnt/','common',4.18,'plain','["noun", "verb"]','A roll of lint or linen, or a conical or cylindrical piece of sponge or other absorbent, used chiefly to dilate a natural canal, to keep open the orifice of a wound, or to absorb discharges.','noun','From Middle English tente (“a probe”), from Middle French tente, deverbal of tenter, from Latin tentāre (“to probe, test”), alteration of temptāre (“to test, probe, tempt”).',173,'120_200',1,0.8,419),
