('matutine','matutine',NULL,'/məˈtu.tɪn/','rare',0.12,'plain','["adjective"]','Of or relating to early morning; occurring in the early morning; matutinal.','adjective','From Latin matutinus (“pertaining to morning”), from Matuta (“Roman goddess of the morning”); related to Latin maturus (“early”) (compare mature). By surface analysis, Matuta + -ine.',182,'120_200',1,0.65,426),
