('catback','catback',NULL,NULL,'scarce',1.17,'plain','["noun"]','The totality of components which exhaust gases flow through after exiting a vehicle''s catalytic converter.','noun','From cat + back, sense 2 (the back of a cat, for riding upon) is modelled on horseback.',87,'80_120',0,0.5,428),
('intermezzo','intermezzo',NULL,'/ɪntɚˈmɛtsoʊ/','uncommon',2.26,'plain','["noun"]','A short piece of music or act in the interval of the main spectacle; a theatrical interlude.','noun','Borrowed from Italian intermezzo. Doublet of intermede and intermedium',70,'40_80',1,0.58,429),
('Mountain Province','Mountain Province',NULL,'/ˌmaʊ̯n.tɛn ˈpɾa.vɪns/','rare',NULL,'multiword,capitalized','["proper noun"]','A province of the Cordillera Administrative Region, Luzon, Philippines. Capital: Bontoc.','proper noun','Formerly Spanish La Montañosa.',30,'lt40',1,0.35,430),
('lazurite','lazurite',NULL,NULL,'scarce',1.04,'plain','["noun"]','A mineral of metamorphosed limestones. Lazurite forms the gemstone lapis lazuli, and crushed lazurite provided the ultramarine color in artists'' paint of the Old Masters. Sodalite and lazurite form the sodalite group of silicate minerals. Chemical composition: Sodium aluminum silicate with sulphur, Na₄₋₅Al₃Si₃O₁₂S.','noun','From Medieval Latin lazur (“lapis lazuli”) (from Arabic لَازَوَرْد (lāzaward), from Persian لاژورد (lâžvard)) + -ite.',117,'80_120',1,0.65,431),
('consistent','consistent',NULL,'/kənˈsɪs.tənt/','common',4.72,'plain','["noun", "adjective"]','Of a regularly occurring, dependable nature.','adjective','Borrowed from Latin cōnsistēntem, present participle of cōnsistō (“to agree with; to continue”), from con- (prefix indicating a being or bringing together of several objects) (ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *ḱóm (“beside, by, near, with”)) + sistō (“to cause to stand; to place, set”) (ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *stísteh₂ti (“to be standing up; to be getting up”), from the root *steh₂- (“to stand (up)”)). By surface analysis, consist + -ent.',458,'200plus',1,0.8,432),
('calcigerous','calcigerous',NULL,NULL,'obscure',-0.61,'plain','["adjective"]','Containing lime.','adjective','From Latin calcis (“genitive singular of calx (chalk, limestone)”) + -gerous (“bearing”); compare calciferous.',110,'80_120',1,0.55,433),
