('zero-grade','zero-grade',NULL,NULL,'rare',NULL,'hyphenated','["noun"]','In Proto-Indo-European linguistics, an ablaut form of a root characterized by the absence of the basic ablauting vowel phonemes */e/ and */o/.','noun','From zero + grade, as in gradation (“apophony”). Possibly after German Nullstufe.',81,'80_120',1,0.55,484),
