('bluff','bluff',1,'/blʌf/','common',3.68,'plain','["noun", "verb"]','An act of bluffing; a false expression of the strength of one’s position in order to intimidate or deceive; braggadocio.','noun','Probably from Dutch bluffen (“to brag”), from Middle Dutch bluffen (“to make something swell; to bluff”); or from the Dutch noun bluf (“bragging”). Related to German verblüffen (“to stump, perplex”).',199,'120_200',1,0.8,499),
('béarnaise sauce','béarnaise sauce',NULL,NULL,'rare',NULL,'multiword,nonascii','["noun"]','A sauce made of clarified butter emulsified in egg yolks and white wine vinegar and flavored with herbs.','noun','from French, the feminine of béarnais (the adjective from the Béarn region, using -ais (“-ese”)) + sauce',104,'80_120',1,0.55,500);
